/-!
# Experimental Jensen-wedge research interface

Exact finite algebra, the concrete T1 xi/theta coefficient identity, the
concrete T2 sectorial saddle branch, the complete T3 leading contour theorem,
the complete T4 all-mode contour theorem, and a conditional proof firewall
are exported.  The complete theta moment including the low-end Mellin
interval and its exact positive-integer coefficient assembly are also kernel
checked, together with the exact holomorphic differential identities, the
fixed-inner-sector two-shift ratio for the nonzero saddle main term, and an
effective positive-integer Stirling anchor. The normalized complex Gamma
quotient, its `3/(Re z)^2` logarithmic-derivative bound, and its integrated
fixed-sector `1/|z|` relative-error theorem are concrete. The full theta
Mellin moment, exact coefficient continuation, displayed main, and combined
relative error are holomorphic on the paired coefficient sector, with the
paper's proportional-disc Cauchy transport through order six. The exact
Gamma-factor removal to the manuscript auxiliary moment is also kernel
checked and preserves that same relative error. Concrete residual/Jacobian
branch enclosures and the two general finite-free literature theorems remain
open. Their finite convention, localization-adapter, and typed assembly
consequences are exported.  The concrete xi multiplier, its exact six node
values, uniform tube bound, finite Newton estimate, canonical Rolle interval
certificate, and the final Riemann-xi Jensen root theorem are kernel checked;
the headline theorem is conditional only on the explicitly typed
Jacobi/MSS/MMP literature inputs.
